<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Alo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alo is one of the two traditional kingdoms of the island of Futuna in the French Pacific territory of Wallis and Futuna, covering the eastern part of Futuna and the neighbouring island of Alofi. Its king, the Tu'i Agaifo, is chosen from noble families. Alo accepted a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1888, and its king is recognised in the territory's statute of 1961.</p></div>
